\label{def:CtsAbBund}
Let $\mathrm{B}$ be an abelian bundle with base $S$, structure group $\mathrm{Z}$ and projection $\pi$. We say that $\mathrm{B}$ is  \emph{continuous} if the following conditions hold:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\mathrm{B}$ and $S$ are topological spaces.
\item $\mathrm{Z}$ is an abelian topological group.
\item The action $\alpha:\mathrm{Z}\times \mathrm{B}\rightarrow \mathrm{B}$ is continuous.
\item A set $U\subset S$ is open if and only if $\pi^{-1}(U)$ is open in $\mathrm{B}$.
\end{enumerate}

On the translation bundle $\mathcal{T}$ we will have two different actions of $\mathrm{Z}_k$. If we let $(x_0,x_1)\in \mathcal{T}$ then we have on the one hand the diagonal action of $\mathrm{Z}_k$, given by $((x_0,x_1),z)\mapsto (x_0+z,x_1+z)$. And on the other hand, we have the addition on the second component $((x_0,x_1),z)\mapsto (x_0,x_1+z)$. Consider now the  commutative diagram
\[
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \matrix (m) [matrix of math nodes,row sep=2em,column sep=4em,minimum width=2em]
  {\mathcal{T} & \mathrm{X}  \\
     \mathcal{T}_{k-1} & \mathrm{X}_{k-1}.\\};
  \path[-stealth]
    (m-1-1) edge node [above] {$q$} (m-1-2)
    (m-1-1) edge node [right] {$\pi$} (m-2-1)
    (m-1-2) edge node [right] {$\pi$} (m-2-2)
    (m-2-1) edge node [above] {$q_{k-1}$} (m-2-2);
\end{tikzpicture}
\]

\vspace{-0.3cm}

\noindent The diagonal action makes $\mathcal{T}$ a degree-$k$ extension over $\mathcal{T}_{k-1}$ whereas the addition on the second component makes $\mathcal{T}$ a degree-$(k-i)$ extension over $\mathrm{X}$.

