\label{lem:top-degree-k-k-ext}
Let $\mathrm{X}$ be a $k$-step \textsc{lch} nilspace. Let $\mathrm{Y}$ be a degree-$k$ algebraic nilspace extension of $\mathrm{X}$ by an abelian group $\mathrm{Z}$, with corresponding fibration $q:\mathrm{Y}\rightarrow\mathrm{X}$. Suppose that $\mathrm{Y},\mathrm{Z}$ are equipped with \textsc{lch} topologies making $\mathrm{Y}$ a Cartan continuous $\mathrm{Z}$-bundle over $\mathrm{X}$. Suppose also that the following  hold:
\setlength{\leftmargini}{0.8cm}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item For every $n\geq 0$ the cube set $\mathrm{C}^n(\mathrm{Y})$ is a closed subset of $\mathrm{Y}^{\db{n}}$.
    \item The completion function $\mathcal{K}:\mathrm{Cor}^{k+1}(\mathrm{Y})\rightarrow \mathrm{Y}$ is continuous.
\end{enumerate}
Then $\mathrm{Y}$ is an \textsc{lch} nilspace.

\label{thm:ext-lch-nil}
Let $\mathrm{X}$ be a $k$-step \textsc{lch} nilspace. Let $\mathrm{Y}$ be a degree-$t$ algebraic nilspace extension of $\mathrm{X}$ by an abelian group $\mathrm{Z}$, with corresponding fibration $q:\mathrm{Y}\rightarrow\mathrm{X}$. Suppose that $\mathrm{Y}$, $\mathrm{Z}$ are equipped with \textsc{lch} topologies making $\mathrm{Y}$ a Cartan continuous $\mathrm{Z}$-bundle over $\mathrm{X}$. Suppose also that the following hold:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item For every $n\geq 0$ the cube set $\mathrm{C}^n(\mathrm{Y})$ is a closed subset of $\mathrm{Y}^{\db{n}}$.
    \item The completion function $\mathcal{K}:\mathrm{Cor}^{k+1}(\mathrm{Y})\rightarrow \mathrm{Y}$ is continuous.
    \item The extension is fiber-completion continuous.
\end{enumerate}
Then $\mathrm{Y}$ is an \textsc{lch} nilspace.

