if it satisfies property \eqref{eq:ft-fil}. A subgroup $\Gamma$ of $\Theta(\mathrm{X})$ will be said to be \emph{fiber-transitive on} $\mathrm{X}$ if the filtration $(\Gamma\cap \Theta_i(\mathrm{X}))_{i\geq 0}$ is fiber-transitive on $\mathrm{X}$.

