The lattice $\Gamma_k=\ker(\pi)$ is finitely generated, so let $z_1,\ldots,z_t\in \mathrm{Z}_k'$ form a generating set for $\Gamma_k$. Then for every $s\in[t]$ let $\gamma_s\in \Theta_k(F)$ be the map $\gamma_s(f,a'):=(f,a'+z_s)$  (recall that $(f,a')\in F=F_{k-1}\times \mathcal{D}_k(\mathrm{Z}_k')$). 


We claim that the filtered group $\big(H':=\langle h_1'\ldots,h_n',\gamma_1,\ldots,\gamma_t\rangle,\; H'_\bullet:=(H'\cap\Theta_i(F))_{i\geq 0}\big)$, together with the map $\varphi:=p_2\circ\hspace{-0.02 cm} \iota^{-1}\circ\hspace{-0.02 cm} \phi: F\rightarrow \mathrm{X}$, satisfy the conclusion of the theorem. 

